DANA on the read-back: Inspection first: seven in ten is right. "Catches pretty much everything" was loose talk.

On the close call, I'd bid at $48,000 with complete records, even from a contractor. Complete records matter more than the seller type, so the fleet condition gives way, and the forty-five line is soft.

On max bid, it's the hammer price, and I take expected repairs off too, so it's about $63,000 on that excavator, not $66,000. Win right at that and the margin is thin, a few grand after premium and transport. I usually win under it.

The other points I'd have to think about.
CONSULTANT: I changed the max bid to about $63,000 hammer on the excavator, made the forty-five line soft, and recorded that complete records would have made you bid at $48,000 even from a contractor; the seven in ten stays. Is anything else wrong?

